      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments): any comment employs a specific, verifiable procedural example (concrete named/described process, rule, procedure or case of how something is actually done that could be checked)",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list for the row (comments by users other than the OP). Return 1 if at least one comment itself employs a specific, verifiable procedural example: a concrete, particular instance or description of an actual procedure, process, rule, protocol or practice (e.g. how a legal, administrative, scientific or institutional process actually works or worked in a specific case) that could in principle be checked, as support for its rebuttal. Illustrative examples are nonexhaustive. Do not require outside verification; judge only from the supplied text. Vague generalities, hypotheticals and purely abstract/theoretical reasoning do not count. Ignore quoted OP text. Return 0 if the list is valid and no comment does so (including valid empty list). Return null if OC_comments is missing or malformed. Do not use any other columns.  "
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 90,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_cites_empirical_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments): any comment makes a specific counter-argument that cites an empirical example",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the JSON list in OC_comments (comments by users other than OP). Return 1 if at least one comment presents a specific counter-argument against the OP's view that cites a concrete empirical example (e.g., a specific real-world case, event, study, statistic, or documented observation) in support. Examples are nonexhaustive; no external verification needed. Purely abstract, hypothetical, or opinion-only reasoning does not count. Return 0 if the list is valid and no comment qualifies. Empty list gives 0. Null if OC_comments is missing or malformed. Do not use other columns."
    }
  }
